        "id": "svelte.component-size",
        "description": "Component longer than 300 lines; split it",
        "enabled": true,
        "scope": "file",
        "paths": [
          "src/renderer/**/*.svelte"
        ],
        "exclude_paths": [],
        "severity": "minor",
        "locate": false,
        "min_confidence": 0.5,
        "guard": false,
        "candidate_removed": false,
        "type": "file_lines",
        "max_lines": 300,
        "report_existing": false
      },
      {
        "id": "svelte.effect-as-derived",
        "description": "$effect only derives a value from other state; use $derived",
        "enabled": true,
        "scope": "hunk",
        "paths": [
          "src/renderer/**/*.svelte",
          "src/renderer/**/*.svelte.ts"
        ],
        "exclude_paths": [],
        "severity": "minor",
        "instructions": "Is there an added Svelte `$effect(() => { ... })` block in `changes.lines` whose body only computes values from reactive state and assigns them to local variables, with no other effect (no DOM access, no API, store or network call, no events, no timers, no async work)? Such a value should be declared with $derived instead.",
        "locate": true,
        "min_confidence": 0.5,
        "guard": false,
        "candidate_removed": false,
        "type": "noul",
        "criteria": {
          "true": "For example $effect(() => { count = items.length }) or $effect(() => { visible = list.filter((x) => x.open) }). Calls to get...() functions such as getToolView() or getTrackerCredentials() only read reactive store state and have no side effects.",
          "false": "No $effect is added, or the effect does something besides computing local values: it touches the DOM or focus, calls an API, a store method or a function that loads data, dispatches an event, writes to shared state outside the component, runs async code, starts a timer, or initializes state once behind a guard flag."
        },
        "fires_on": "yes",
        "threshold": 0.7
      }
